course: dictionary
lesson: 112
title: Admire: to think well of someone
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To admire someone is to think they are very good, clever or brave, and to respect them. To admire something is to look at it with pleasure because it is beautiful or well made. Admire is a verb, so its forms are admire, admires, admired and admiring.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. In Bradford, about 20 aunties pinch Hamid's cheeks and say, «Mashallah, so big now!» «Mashallah» is said to admire something good, so the aunties are showing they think well of him, even though the pinching is squeezy and he is fed up.
explain: Admiring someone does not mean you always agree with them or like everything they do. «A person can be scared of someone and admire them at the same time.» Try the swap check: put «think well of» in place of admire. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Admire means to think someone is very good, clever or brave, or to look at something with pleasure.
fact: «The Rat admires the little sleeping-bunks in the wall» means he looks at them with pleasure because they are nice.
fact: Greta Thunberg, Malala Yousafzai and the students of March for Our Lives are people many admire, although many disagree with what they ask for.
fact: Useful phrases: admire the view, look up to someone, and «I admire you for» your courage or kindness.
fact: You can admire someone and still disagree with them. Both can be true at once.
exercise: «The Rat stopped to admire the little sleeping-bunks in the wall.» What does admire mean here? | *To look at them with pleasure because they are nice | To count them | To run away from them | To paint them black
exercise: «I admire you for your courage.» What does admire mean in this sentence? | To forget you quickly | *To think you are brave and respect you | To copy everything you do | To be annoyed with you
exercise: Nadia says, «I can be scared of my teacher and still admire her.» Is that possible? | Yes, but only if she is a famous explorer | *Yes, you can be scared of someone and admire them at the same time | No, admire only means to laugh at someone | No, admiring someone means you can never feel fear
test: Malala Yousafzai spoke up for girls' education, and many people admire her. What does admire mean here? | *To think she is brave and respect her | To feel sorry for her and forget her | To be bored of her | To sell her books
test: Which form of admire is the past tense? | *admired | admires | admire | admiring
exam: Which sentence uses admire to mean to think well of someone? | The Rat sleeps in the wall | *Many people admire Greta Thunberg, even though many disagree with what she asks for | Hamid goes to a wedding and gets his cheeks pinched | The servo is closed, love
